[00:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hi everyone, Liam here for Archipelago Presets&nbsp; and in this video I’ll be doing an unboxing and&nbsp;&nbsp; early review of the Sotsu FlipAction Elite 16&nbsp; inch Portable Monitor an aluminium enclosure&nbsp;&nbsp; 4k monitor with some very clever tricks&nbsp; up it’s sleeve. I picked this up to use&nbsp;&nbsp; both as a second display when on the go and&nbsp; also as a third display for my desktop setup&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to maximise productivity and workflow and while&nbsp; it’s not cheap coming in at £730 here in the UK,&nbsp;&nbsp; there really isn’t any other monitor&nbsp; currently on the market that offers&nbsp;&nbsp; everything that this one does, so let’s&nbsp; get into the unboxing and take a look.'

[00:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'As you can see it’s packaged really nicely in&nbsp; this minimal and clean box. Opening it up we&nbsp;&nbsp; can see that it comes with this nice simple&nbsp; neoprene sleeve that’s going to help protect&nbsp;&nbsp; the monitor when travelling. And here we have&nbsp; the monitor itself flipping it over we can see&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that the built in kickstand has multiple IO&nbsp; ports including a mini HDMI and USB Type-c&nbsp;&nbsp; for connecting your device, there’s a type-c&nbsp; power in to allow power-passthrough when using&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it with something like a phone, and an SD slot,&nbsp; plus a 4 way control button on the top left. On the right hand side we have the kickstand base,&nbsp;&nbsp; which conveniently attaches magnetically to&nbsp; the back of the display while transporting it.'

[01:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Peeling off the stickers here we can see&nbsp; the fully aluminium enclosure which gives&nbsp;&nbsp; it a really premium look and feel and we’ve&nbsp; got that nice clean Sotsu branding at the&nbsp;&nbsp; base of the kickstand. Also included&nbsp; in the box is a USB-C to USB-C cable&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which is all you need to connect it to&nbsp; a computer, no external power supply&nbsp;&nbsp; necessary. And we have a user manual with&nbsp; instructions for setting up the monitor.'

[01:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'My first impressions are that every part&nbsp; of this device feels premium and well made,&nbsp;&nbsp; the kickstand feels firm and sturdy and&nbsp; you can actually use the display with&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just the built in stand. The&nbsp; kickstand base feels equally&nbsp;&nbsp; as sturdy and firm and has a rubber&nbsp; base to keep it from sliding around. Once the monitor is mounted by simply slotting the&nbsp; kickstand into the base it essentially becomes a&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mini Studio Display and this is where it really&nbsp; comes alive. As well as being able to tilt the&nbsp;&nbsp; display you can rotate the screen up to 180&nbsp; degrees giving options for a vertical display&nbsp;&nbsp; as well as this raised horizontal position&nbsp; that’s perfect for a stacked display setup&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with a laptop as you can see here with my 16&nbsp; inch macbook pro. Now if I connect up the usb-c&nbsp;&nbsp; into my mac and then into the main port on&nbsp; the stand the display immediately powers up.&nbsp;&nbsp; Once it’s on I can use the four way control to&nbsp; adjust brightness and change picture settings.'

[02:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I found the display to be very well&nbsp; calibrated straight out of the box with&nbsp;&nbsp; only the brightness just needing decreasing&nbsp; a little bit from the default to better match&nbsp;&nbsp; my preference. As mentioned this is a 4k&nbsp; display with a resolution of 3840 x 2400px,&nbsp;&nbsp; a max brightness of 450 nits,&nbsp; a contrast ration of 1200:1,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'full DCI-P3 colour gamut making it a great choice&nbsp; for photo and video work, and a 60Hz refresh rate. Here’s a look at it in vertical&nbsp; orientation which I really enjoy.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'When you rotate the display you can either&nbsp; rotate clockwise or anti-clockwise which&nbsp;&nbsp; places the stand on the right or the&nbsp; left depending on your preference. Packing down the display is a breeze, simply&nbsp; remove the monitor from the kickstand base,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fold the base and attach it magnetically to&nbsp; the back of the display, it fits perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp; and the magnet is nice and strong so no&nbsp; worries about that falling off. Slide&nbsp;&nbsp; it into the neoprene sleeve, grab&nbsp; your cable and you’re good to go.'

[03:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For my desktop setup I’ve chosen to&nbsp; use the monitor without the base,&nbsp;&nbsp; just flipping out the kickstand and placing it&nbsp; directly beneath my Pro Display XDR giving me&nbsp;&nbsp; a 3 monitor setup which I find incredibly&nbsp; useful for video editing and other tasks&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:39] [scene:talk]
